**Financing and leasing business** (also called “finance and leasing business”) covers the business of providing credit facilities of any kind for consideration (including interest). This explicitly includes instalment credit for hire purchase, leasing (other than any lease granting exclusive rights to occupy land), conditional sale, or credit sale. It excludes banking business, fund management, and (in KY) financial leasing of land or an interest in land. [1][2][4]

Core income-generating activities listed for this relevant activity are:
- agreeing funding terms;
- identifying and acquiring assets to be leased (leasing cases);
- setting the terms and duration of any financing or leasing;
- monitoring and revising agreements;
- managing any risks. [3][6]

These definitions and activities appear consistently across the KY, JE and VG sources provided. No further detail is given in the excerpts.
